questions.question:
If for the matrix, $$A = \left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; { - \alpha }  \cr 
   \alpha  &amp; \beta   \cr 

 } } \right]$$, $$A{A^T} = {I_2}$$, then the value of $${\alpha ^4} + {\beta ^4}$$ is :

questions.explanation:
$$\left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; { - \alpha }  \cr 
   \alpha  &amp; \beta   \cr 

 } } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; \alpha   \cr 
   { - \alpha } &amp; \beta   \cr 

 } } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
   {1 + {\alpha ^2}} &amp; {\alpha  - \alpha \beta }  \cr 
   {\alpha  - \alpha \beta } &amp; {{\alpha ^2} + {\beta ^2}}  \cr 

 } } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
   1 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right]$$

1 + $$\alpha$$<sup>2</sup> = 1

$$\alpha$$<sup>2</sup> = 0

$$\alpha$$<sup>2</sup> + $$\beta$$<sup>2</sup> = 1

$$\beta$$<sup>2</sup> = 1

$$\alpha$$<sup>4</sup> = 0

$$\beta$$<sup>4</sup> = 1

$$\alpha$$<sup>4</sup> + $$\beta$$<sup>4</sup> = 1

$$\Delta  = \left| {\matrix{
   2 &amp; 3 &amp; 2  \cr 
   3 &amp; 2 &amp; 2  \cr 
   1 &amp; { - 1} &amp; 4  \cr 

 } } \right| =  - 20 \ne 0$$ $$ \therefore $$ unique solution

$${\Delta _x} = \left| {\matrix{
   9 &amp; 3 &amp; 2  \cr 
   9 &amp; 2 &amp; 2  \cr 
   8 &amp; { - 1} &amp; 4  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0$$

$${\Delta _y} = \left| {\matrix{
   2 &amp; 9 &amp; 2  \cr 
   3 &amp; 9 &amp; 2  \cr 
   1 &amp; 8 &amp; 4  \cr 

 } } \right| =  - 20$$

$${\Delta _z} = \left| {\matrix{
   2 &amp; 3 &amp; 9  \cr 
   3 &amp; 2 &amp; 9  \cr 
   1 &amp; { - 1} &amp; 8  \cr 

 } } \right| =  - 40$$

$$ \therefore $$ $$x = {{{\Delta _x}} \over \Delta } = 0$$

$$y = {{{\Delta _y}} \over \Delta } = 1$$

$$z = {{{\Delta _z}} \over \Delta } = 2$$

Unique solution : (0, 1, 2)

